{"skill":{"slug":"mx-finance-data","displayName":"All-Market Financial Data Hub"},"version":{"version":"1.0.12","createdAt":1780658980664,"changelog":"mx-finance-data 1.0.12\n\n- Added new files: a compiled Python script and a sample Excel file.\n- Removed the skill-card.md file.\n- SKILL.md: Cleaned up documentation by removing environment setup, security, and registration details; condensed and restructured the feature description for clarity.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6307,"sha256":"17fbaa5eb5539680c597ef8ec6f2777a99d8e7a0d1e3a2ce4c660c2d671a6410","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/get_data.py","size":34751,"sha256":"465e331ce8c1961b00bc53558b974b39bbabc4c32e94f2eaae3c99525daec785","contentType":"text/x-python"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2285,"sha256":"2903366bde27f85e49bbb08ec20dd33fefe15271c03deb81863f1f2b36371329","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789172741716,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"dda4a4162b72b15b9486699ea8aded6cf9ca40448a2c9d0ae537a7aae553f5bc","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/dda4a4162b72b15b9486699ea8aded6cf9ca40448a2c9d0ae537a7aae553f5bc","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780659107827},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":31,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789172741716},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is a coherent finance-data query tool, but an undocumented Python endpoint override can expose the user's Eastmoney API key if invoked with an untrusted URL.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Requiring EM_API_KEY and network access to Eastmoney is proportionate for the purpose, but the endpoint override path can send that credential and query data outside the expected Eastmoney service.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation uses established Python packages through OpenClaw metadata and a documented pip --user command, but versions and hashes are not pinned.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Normal CLI usage is narrowly described as --query and --indicators, yet the broader Python API is less constrained and lacks explicit host allowlisting for authenticated requests.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No background service, scheduled task, tool hijack, or destructive persistence was found; the only persistence-like instruction is user-directed shell profile configuration for EM_API_KEY and local result-file creation.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, Eastmoney API use, financial query handling, and Excel/Markdown outputs fit together, but the script also exposes api_base and entity_api_base parameters that are not documented for users and can redirect credential-bearing requests.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust the Eastmoney API workflow and can protect or revoke the EM_API_KEY. Use the documented CLI path, avoid passing custom API endpoint parameters, and prefer an isolated Python environment with reviewed dependency versions.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Environment access, outbound network calls, and local output files are expected for this finance-data retrieval skill, but explicit network/output scoping would reduce ambiguity.\n[SQP-1] expected: The description is broad across financial markets, but that breadth is consistent with the advertised finance-query purpose rather than evidence of unrelated behavior.\n[SQP-3] expected: The main instructions and CLI text are mostly Chinese, with an English description also present; this is a usability and locale disclosure issue for an Eastmoney-focused skill, not a malicious behavior signal.\n[T09] unexpected: The credential-bearing endpoint override is not needed for ordinary documented CLI use and should be fixed or host-validated before users rely on imported Python API use.\n[T08] expected: The unpinned dependencies are common packages and installed without system privilege, but reproducible pinned dependencies would be safer.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789172741716}}}}}